── NO SUCH METHOD OR MEMBER ─────────── E0314_misspelled_method.lt:1:46  [E0314]

`List<str>` has no method `contians`:

  1 │ fn has_ana(names: List<str>) -> bool { names.contians("ana") }
    │                                              ^^^^^^^^

Check the method's name and the receiver's type. A function without `self` is
named on its type, as `List.new()`, and a trait's method needs an impl of the
trait for the type.

To fix it, write `contains`:

  1 │ fn has_ana(names: List<str>) -> bool { names.contains("ana") }
    │                                              ~~~~~~~~
